s `PathError` to format it correctly for compatibility.\n\nLooking at the requirements, I only need to implement R1.1 through R1.4, which covers basic file concatenation and exit status handling. The task doesn't include automated tests, just build verification and manual testing, so I should focus on clean implementation of the core functionality rather than getting caught up in edge cases like `--help` and `--version` flags.\n\nDefining the main structure with proper signal handling, argument parsing that defaults to stdin when no files are provided, and exit code management that tracks whether any file read operations failed.\n\nWriting the file handling logic... Writing the cat implementation... I'm verifying the implementation against the requirements—checking that file reading works, stdin handling is correct, multiple files concatenate in order, and the exit status behaves properly. All the functions are appropriately sized and the copyright header is in place. The only file needed is cmd/cat/main.go, and I should confirm whether the cmd/cat/ directory already exists in the repository.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":145151,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":145151},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a41a7c22-ba16-41ab-b7a9-8649e81288c3","uuid":"9e1cdb65-9a39-4aa0-9a6a-b91d2b77a52f"}
